    "preview_note": "Fabrinet enters the Q4 FY26 print with strong momentum driven by rapid scaling in AI-driven optical transceivers (800G/1.6T) and high-performance computing interconnect assemblies. We project Q4 FY26 revenue of $1,275M (midpoint of $1,250M\u2013$1,290M guidance) and non-GAAP EPS of $3.77 (vs. $3.72\u2013$3.87 guidance range). Key focus areas for the print will be: (1) Datacom trajectory and progress on onboarding new customer programs; (2) Non-optical HPC segment ramp; and (3) Q1 FY27 guidance, which we expect to guide solidly higher to $1.30B\u2013$1.34B.",
